You are a senior front-end developer working on the TM Hospitality Strategies marketing site: a vanilla HTML/CSS/JS static page deployed to GitHub Pages. No framework and no runtime dependencies; `package.json` only pins the build and test tooling.

## Structure

```
index.html            # Single page, all sections, inline icon sprite, pre-paint theme snippet
404.html              # Error page (uses <base href="/Github-Pages-Demo-1/">)
manifest.webmanifest  # Web app manifest
sw.js                 # Service worker source; stage.cjs fills VERSION, only the build registers it, nothing is precached
tools/*/index.html    # One page per calculator; shared blocks synced from index.html
css/tokens.css        # Fonts, brand tokens, fluid scales, light/dark themes
css/base.css          # Reset, typography, layout, buttons, reveal rules
css/components.css    # All components and responsive rules
js/theme.js           # Theme toggle
js/calc-math.js       # Pure calculator maths (TMHSCalc) + TMHSTools registry; load first
js/calc-prime.js      # Prime cost tool
js/calc-tracker.js    # Prime cost month tracker (localStorage only on explicit save)
js/calc-recipe.js     # Plate + cocktail cost tools (one shared row tool, <template> rows)
js/calc-breakeven.js  # Break-even tool
js/calc-foodcost.js   # Actual vs theoretical food cost tool
js/calc-menu.js       # Your menu: saved plate/cocktail costings and menu engineering (localStorage only on explicit save)
js/calc-tabs.js       # Toolkit tabs, ?tool= shared links, copy link
js/inquiry.js         # Contact message builder, CONTACT_EMAIL
js/main.js            # Menu, reveal, nav spy, parallax, marquee, quick-contact bar
assets/               # fonts/ (self-hosted), images/ (logo, icons, og-image)
tests/smoke.cjs       # Browser test runner; checks live in tests/browser/<area>.cjs (npm test -- <area> runs one)
scripts/              # stage.cjs (publishable build), sync-tool-pages.cjs, check-links.cjs, screenshots.cjs
.github/workflows/    # ci.yml (checks, then deploy of the tested _site)
```

## Rules

- Brand colors and fonts come from the TM Hospitality Strategies Canva brand kit. Use the CSS custom properties in `:root`; never hardcode new colors.
- Do not invent testimonials, statistics, client names or credentials. Placeholder copy must be labeled and marked `TODO(verify)`.
- Semantic HTML, visible focus states, `alt` on every image, AA contrast, `prefers-reduced-motion` respected.
- No third-party scripts, analytics or cookies without updating the README privacy section.
- The Pages artifact is built by `scripts/stage.cjs` (site files only, CSS bundled and minified); add new top-level site files there.
- Blocks between `<!-- sync:NAME -->` markers in index.html (sprite, header, footer, tool panels, row templates) are copied into tools/*/index.html. Edit them in index.html only, then run `npm run sync`.
- tools/tools.json holds the site's address (`site`), the tool registry and other pages (`pages`, e.g. privacy/); never hard-code the address elsewhere.
- privacy/index.html describes what the site collects and stores. Update it before adding anything that collects or stores data (analytics, forms, new localStorage).
- tools/tools.json is the tool registry. `<!-- gen:NAME -->` blocks (tool links, other-tools lists, embed snippets, credits), sitemap.xml and the manifest shortcuts are generated from it by `npm run sync`; never edit them by hand.
- Prime cost bands: BANDS in js/calc-math.js is the source; the calculator note, the prime cost explainer and scripts/make-tracker-template.py (the spreadsheet) repeat them, and tests/bands.test.cjs fails until they agree.
- Validate before committing: `npm ci` once, then `npm run check`.
- Shapes: buttons, tabs, fields and chips use `--radius-ctl` (6px), badges `--radius-tag`; no pill (999px) controls. Cards use `--radius` / `--radius-l`.
- No inline `style` attributes (html-validate rejects them); use classes. Use design tokens, never hardcoded colors.
- Stage files by name; never `git add -A` (scratch screenshots and Playwright output must not be committed).
